<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 467.9 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 467.9 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of January 23 raised 467.9 billion Lebanese pounds ($302.7 million), the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 516.6 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 176 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.17 (14.21)	   34   (53.7)</p>
<p>    Six months		15.89 (16.01)	  133   (239.2)</p>
<p>    12 months		 16.38 (16.76)	   92.9 (83.2)</p>
<p>    24 months		 18.12 (18.70)	  208   (140.5)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,550.25 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,550.75 a week earlier and 1,592 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
<p>($ = 1545 Lebanese Pounds)</p>
